Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.319
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar and you're watching 'Mind Your Decisions'

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:07.319
Here's a really fun problem

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:14.160
Solve 615 plus x squared is equal to 2 to the power of y, over the integers

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.789
You're not allowed to use computers or calculators.

00:00:18.789 --> 00:00:25.559
I thank Luka Khizambareli from Georgia for suggesting this problem and for sending a solution

00:00:26.199 --> 00:00:28.199
Can you figure it out?

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:33.119
Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for a solution

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.170
So, how can we solve this equation

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.379
Well, I'll admit that I did not solve this problem

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.739
So I resorted to WolframAlpha

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:01.459
You can solve equations for integer solutions

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:07.699
For example, if you type solve 3x plus 4y is equal to five over the integers Wolfram

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:14.089
Alpha will give you examples of integer solutions. So I thought: since I'm not able to solve this problem

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:17.059
Maybe I can get the result from WolframAlpha

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:23.570
So I typed it in and to my great surprise it said the result is false

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:31.009
The examples of integer solutions it gave were not actual solutions to this equation over the integers

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:36.530
So this is wrong. The problem actually does have the solution

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:42.499
So now let's proceed to solve a problem that WolframAlpha is not yet able to solve

00:01:43.679 --> 00:01:45.450
How can we do that?

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:50.539
We'll start with the basic observation. Since x squared is non-negative

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:54.900
2 to the power of y is at least 615

00:01:55.530 --> 00:02:01.940
We can then conclude y is greater than 9 because 2 to the power of 9 is equal to 512

00:02:03.569 --> 00:02:08.359
We then proceed by considering that if this equation has a solution

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:12.739
Both sides need to have the same last digit

00:02:13.319 --> 00:02:18.289
So we'll analyze the very last digit of 615 plus x squared

00:02:18.959 --> 00:02:23.779
We'll start out by considering X. The very last digit it could have is from 0 to 9

00:02:24.959 --> 00:02:32.809
So then we consider the last digit of x squared. We take the square of each of these digits and consider only the last digit

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:41.390
To get the last digit of 615 + x squared, we add 5 to each of the last digits of x squared.

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:46.250
We now consider the very last digit of 2 to the power of y.

00:02:47.819 --> 00:02:56.700
You can figure this out by doing a few calculations. If you calculate the values for y is equal to 1, 2, 3, 4 and so on

00:02:56.790 --> 00:03:04.900
You'll see a pattern: the last digit of 2 to the power of y will follow a pattern 2, 4, 8, 6

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:10.999
then the pattern will repeat 2, 4, 8, 6 and so on for every four numbers

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:15.829
Now in order that the last digits match

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:22.009
We look at the last digit of 615 plus x squared and we want to see which ones

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:24.440
correspond to 2, 4, 8 or 6

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:32.809
This only happens when x is equal to 1, 3, 7 or 9 and the last digit will be 6 or 4

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:42.019
So for the digits to match the very last digits x would have to be 1, 3, 7 or 9 and

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:50.029
y would have to be 2, 4, 6, 8 and so on. In other words y would have to be an even number

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:56.030
So we've established that y is even and that'll be the key to solving this problem

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:59.250
Why does this help us?

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:05.660
Well, if y is even that means y is equal to 2 times n, for n an integer

00:04:06.359 --> 00:04:08.100
We can then substitute

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:15.229
2 to the (*times) n for y. So we have 615 plus x squared is equal to 2 to the power of 2 n

00:04:16.049 --> 00:04:18.379
We then subtract x squared from both sides

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:21.379
And now we use a clever trick

00:04:22.169 --> 00:04:26.149
On the right hand side, we have a difference of squares.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.910
So we can use the difference of squares formula

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:35.299
That a squared minus b squared is equal to the quantity a plus b times the quantity a minus b

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:40.219
In this case we can factor that 615 is equal to the quantity

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:44.989
2 to the n plus x times 2 to then minus x

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.710
So

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.870
We're now going to analyze

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:56.179
615 for two factors: 2 to the n plus x and 2 to the n minus x

00:04:56.970 --> 00:04:59.720
We can do this by considering the prime factorization

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:03.679
615 is equal to 3 times 5 times 41

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:10.969
So we consider which two numbers, what pairs of factors we could have which would equal 615

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:13.460
We can enumerate the possibilities

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:18.479
We can have 1 times 615, we can have 3 times 205

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:23.579
5 times 123 or 15 times 41

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:30.030
Now, how can we figure out which possibility corresponds to our solution?

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.519
We'll consider adding the two factors together

00:05:32.979 --> 00:05:37.079
2 to the n plus x plus 2 to the n minus x will equal

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:42.600
2 times 2 to the n and that simplifies to be 2 to the power of n plus 1

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:47.459
So the sum of the two factors is equal to 2 to the power of n plus 1

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:52.049
So we now consider the sum of the factors in each of these 4 cases

00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:58.380
We need it to be a power of 2 and of these 4 numbers:

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:01.439
only 128 is a power of 2

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:09.000
So the sum of factors, if there's a solution, would be 128, which equals 2 to the power of 7

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.369
which equals 2 to the power of n plus 1

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:18.210
Therefore n is equal to 6 and then y is equal to 2 times n which is 12

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.300
Now with this knowledge, how can we solve for x?

00:06:24.980 --> 00:06:33.160
Well, we can consider the difference of factors. 2 to the n plus x minus the quantity 2 to the n minus x is equal to 2x.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:36.200
And that's the difference of the two factors

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:41.340
So now we take the difference of 123 and 5 and we get 118

00:06:41.979 --> 00:06:47.309
That's equal to 2x which means X is equal to 59. So if there's a solution

00:06:47.979 --> 00:06:55.529
It would have to be X is equal to 59 and Y is equal to 12 and in fact, we can verify that

00:06:56.199 --> 00:06:59.069
615 plus 59 squared is equal to

00:06:59.830 --> 00:07:03.990
4096 which exactly equals 2 to the power of 12 and

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:05.770
for completeness

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:13.349
We should also include X is equal to negative 59 and Y is equal to 12 because integers can be both positive and negative

00:07:13.690 --> 00:07:20.849
And I'll admit this was a solution I overlooked when I first published this video. Thank you all for catching the mistake

00:07:22.510 --> 00:07:26.939
We just solved a problem that WolframAlpha is not yet able to solve

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:32.070
All we did was use the principles of number theories. I think that's pretty neat

00:07:32.800 --> 00:07:34.800
Did you figure it out?

